From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Barry Quokka <354230574+BarryQuokka@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: x126100-lenovo-thinkcentre-neo-50q-qc: Drop
 the second NVMe slot

The neo 50q QC has one M.2 slot, on PCIe 6a: Windows enumerates its NVMe
drive at \_SB.PCI6.RP1.NVME, Gen4 x4, and only PCI4 (Wi-Fi), PCI5
(Ethernet) and PCI6 have devices. The IdeaCentre Mini x dtsi this tree
builds on also enables PCIe 3 for a second slot, and powers both slots'
3.3 V from regulators that share TLMM 18.

On this X1-26-100 (Purwa) the PCIe 3 PHY has no init sequence, so the
controller fails to probe:

  qcom-qmp-pcie-phy 1bd4000.phy: Init sequence not available
  qcom-pcie 1bd0000.pcie: probe with driver qcom-pcie failed with error -61

Unwinding that probe drops VREG_NVME2_3P3, which drives TLMM 18 low and
cuts the power to the real slot while PCIe 6a trains its link. So the
drive is never found, the installer offers no disk, and a sync_state()
stays pending on 1bd0000.pcie for the interconnects and the GCC:

  qcom-pcie 1bf8000.pcie: Device not found
  gpio18 : out low

Turn off PCIe 3, its PHY and the second slot's regulator. With them off,
TLMM 18 stays high and the drive comes up:

  qcom-pcie 1bf8000.pcie: PCIe Gen.4 x4 link up
  nvme0n1: p1 p2 p3 p4

Tested on a ThinkCentre neo 50q QC (13C8) with the Omarchy edge ISO
2026.11.18.495 (linux-omarchy 7.3.0-72), its embedded tree edited the
same way (PCIe 3 and its PHY off, the second regulator unbound).

Signed-off-by: Barry Quokka <354230574+BarryQuokka@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../dts/qcom/x126100-lenovo-thinkcentre-neo-50q-qc.dts | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x126100-lenovo-thinkcentre-neo-50q-qc.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x126100-lenovo-thinkcentre-neo-50q-qc.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x126100-lenovo-thinkcentre-neo-50q-qc.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x126100-lenovo-thinkcentre-neo-50q-qc.dts
@@ -134,6 +134,14 @@
 	link-frequencies = /bits/ 64 <1620000000 2700000000 5400000000>;
 };
 
+&pcie3 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&pcie3_phy {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
 &pcie4_port0 {
 	/delete-node/ wifi@0;
 
@@ -225,6 +233,10 @@
 	};
 };
 
+&vreg_nvme2_3p3 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
 &vreg_v0p9 {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
-- 
